{"id":"ee11792e-6dc8-4390-abf7-a8b1fd62590c","revision":0,"last_node_id":27,"last_link_id":40,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-400],"size":[2900,340],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Edit by scene — picture × picture × instruction (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nThree inputs: the **shots** (Load Media: one named group per scene — *image 1*), the **references** (Load Media: a cat and an umbrella — *image 2*) and one **instruction per reference** (Panel: `# reference` + its instruction, in the same order). Every shot is edited once with every reference: 6 shots × 2 references = 12 edits.\n\n1. **Tree to Data** puts the references into one list, so **Cross Reference** pairs every shot with all of them: each shot becomes a sub-branch `{scene;shot}` holding the shot once per reference (*A*) next to the references (*B*).\n2. A second **Cross Reference** does the same with the instructions — same shots, same order — so in every sub-branch instruction k sits next to reference k.\n3. **XY Lists** in *zip* mode lays the three trees side by side — image 1 on *x*, image 2 on *y*, the instruction on *z* — and the edit model runs once per (shot, reference), seeing both pictures. Its *shape* keeps the shots' branches.\n4. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into `{scene;shot}`; **List Item** `0` takes the untouched shot and **Merge** appends the edits → each row of the **Image Grid** is *original, + cat, + umbrella*, the columns labelled by **Collect** from the references' names. **Save by Path** keeps the structure on disk: `output/arbor/edits/0-0 · Arrival · 1/…`.\n\nUse your own pictures with **Add…** on either Load Media. Add a reference and its instruction (same order) and every shot gets one more edit. In the instructions, call the pictures *image 1* and *image 2*."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Edit by scene — picture × picture × instruction (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nThree inputs: the **shots** (Load Media: one named group per scene — *image 1*), the **references** (Load Media: a cat and an umbrella — *image 2*) and one **instruction per reference** (Panel: `# reference` + its instruction, in the same order). Every shot is edited once with every reference: 6 shots × 2 references = 12 edits.\n\n1. **Tree to Data** puts the references into one list, so **Cross Reference** pairs every shot with all of them: each shot becomes a sub-branch `{scene;shot}` holding the shot once per reference (*A*) next to the references (*B*).\n2. A second **Cross Reference** does the same with the instructions — same shots, same order — so in every sub-branch instruction k sits next to reference k.\n3. **XY Lists** in *zip* mode lays the three trees side by side — image 1 on *x*, image 2 on *y*, the instruction on *z* — and the edit model runs once per (shot, reference), seeing both pictures. Its *shape* keeps the shots' branches.\n4. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into `{scene;shot}`; **List Item** `0` takes the untouched shot and **Merge** appends the edits → each row of the **Image Grid** is *original, + cat, + umbrella*, the columns labelled by **Collect** from the references' names. **Save by Path** keeps the structure on disk: `output/arbor/edits/0-0 · Arrival · 1/…`.\n\nUse your own pictures with **Add…** on either Load Media. Add a reference and its instruction (same order) and every shot gets one more edit. In the instructions, call the pictures *image 1* and *image 2*."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,363],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[1,31]},{"localized_name":"图片","name":"images","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_name":"视频","name":"videos","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_na